  "row_count": 17,
  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase changes: 429.78 K, melting point of In; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 0.780$ kcal/mol. \n660 K, $\\alpha - \\beta$ transition point of $\\mathrm{In}_2\\mathrm{S}_3$ ; $\\Delta \\mathrm{H}^\\circ = 0.270 \\mathrm{kcal} / \\mathrm{mol}$ . \n1100 K, β - γ transition point of $In_{2}S_{3}$ ; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 0.970$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td>298.15-660 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 30.434 + 1.416x $10^{-3}$ T - 2.356x $10^{5}$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td>660-1100 K:</td><td> $H^o$ -  $H_{298}^o$  = 30.434x $10^{-3}$ T + 0.708x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 2.356x $10^{2}$ T $^{-1}$  - 9.927 $Cp^o$  = 23.188 + 13.478x $10^{-3}$ T - 0.100x $10^{5}$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td>1100-1300 K:</td><td> $H^o$ -  $H_{298}^o$  = 23.188x $10^{-3}$ T + 6.739x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 0.100x $10^{2}$ T $^{-1}$  - 7.160 $Cp^o$  = 38.300</td></tr><tr><td></td><td> $H^o$ -  $H_{298}^o$  = 38.300x $10^{-3}$ T - 14.650</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-429.78 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -135.020 + 12.679x10^{-3}T - 9.296x10^{-6}T^{2} + 298.550T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -135.020 - 12.679x10^{-3}T\\ln T + 9.296x10^{-6}T^{2} + 149.275T^{-1} + 151.357x10^{-3}T$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">429.78-660 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -134.301 + 3.985x10^{-3}T + 0.248x10^{-6}T^{2} + 167.150T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -134.301 - 3.985x10^{-3}T\\ln T - 0.248x10^{-6}T^{2} + 83.575T^{-1} + 101.427x10^{-3}T$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">660-1100 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -131.534 - 3.261x10^{-3}T + 6.279x10^{-6}T^{2} - 58.450T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -131.534 + 3.261x10^{-3}T\\ln T - 6.279x10^{-6}T^{2} - 29.225T^{-1} + 54.431x10^{-3}T$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">1100-1300 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -139.024 + 11.851x10^{-3}T - 0.460x10^{-6}T^{2} - 68.450T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -139.024 - 11.851x10^{-3}T\\ln T + 0.460x10^{-6}T^{2} - 34.225T^{-1} + 159.662x10^{-3}T$ </td></tr></table>\nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K from Mills (80). Low-temperature heat capacities and entropy at 298 K from King (68). High-temperature data based on Pankratz (90). ",
